	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<a name="msg16750"></a>
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864" title="View the profile of Zorlo">Zorlo</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Splitpaw Gnoll<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 58<br />
								<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=864"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:Zorlo65@yahoo.com"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1528.msg16750#msg16750"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1528.msg16750#msg16750">Re: pointless cockblocking</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #64 on:</b> May 02, 2005, 06:54:30 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							I just read through this entire post, and one thing that comes to my attention is that mainly High End players, are defending blowing the trigger, and lower end players, are complaining about how it is unfair. I&#039;m sure there are exceptions, but i think this generally shows that high end players are going to support the tactics that got them there, which besides skill and strategy, often include things like, running over lower guilds, and not caring too much about them.<br /><br />Kinsonn brought a legitimate complaint, just that some people who had no business attacking a mob, did so for no reward (other then saying it pushed the envelope or something), and in doing so, prevented lower guilds from accessing one of their viable raid targets. <br /><br />So let&#039;s examine the issue, since i have Mono, and nothing beter to do right now. Toastie, and others claim that that FR is an incredibly easy mob, and is just farmed for daggers. I&#039;ve been on Fennin Ro Raids with Hegemony, Ruination, and Reign of Swords. I&#039;ve seen a Hege raid with 60+ people, and a Ruin raid with 60+ people fail on him, after having completed him before, and being in a much better position gear wise then OA. I&#039;ll admit, he isnt as challenging as many other raid targets, but for a guild of that level, he isn&#039;t exactly a push over. Anyways, that isnt the issue, so claiming that Fennin Ro is trivial, in fact, has absolutley no bearing on whether or not the trigger being blown can be justified, it is called a logical fallacy. <br /><br />Secondly, since i was a member of OA, and have a fairly good idea of their gear standing, i can tell you this: Fennin Ro means more loot wise to OA then a means to get Cudget some fierce new dagger. I seriously doubt the Elemental Molds he drops (Chain Pant, Greaves, Leather Pant, Silk Pant) or the other items he drops are considered a waste of time, and no doubt are sought after, and considered a massive upg for those that win them.<br /><br />There&#039;s also the whole, flagging thing. Before the merger, i&#039;m sure OA would like to get as many flags, for the majority of their membership as they possibly can. And since you can&#039;t get into plane of time without Fennin Ro kills, Fennin Ro is at least as important as any other plane&#039;s target. <br /><br />So that&#039;s what OA lost, potential gear, flags, and advancement of their strategy for attempts.<br /><br />Now, for the other side, we have a group of no doubt industrious individuals who were randomly killing in Fire, for exp or what have you. In keeping with the policy of wanton disruption of a zone, they decided to kill the trigger to test their skills, later adding they meant to attempt the entire sequence. Whether or not they meant to isnt really able to be proven, they didnt act like they wanted to, leaving the zone shortly after killing the trigger, but maybe they did. <br /><br />So, here&#039;s what they gained, the satisfaction of knowing that they could kill a mob with only a handful of hardy adventurers, pushing the envelope of extreme everquesting. Who wouldnt be impressed if you told a story... So we dropped the Harrier in Anguish, and asked ourselves, had we really tested ourselves? No, so we killed a trigger for a few year old mob that was regularly killed by a lower guild to help improve themselves. <br /><br />Even if they meant to continue the script, to kill Fennin Ro, what would they accomplish? Having killed a mob they killed 2 years ago with less people? That&#039;s way hardcore. There was no baby rogue to get ifir either, which i was under the impression was the only reason to kill FR.<br /><br />I realize it is only for 3 days, and that doesn&#039;t justify a huge argument. But it doesn&#039;t justify them having blown the trigger either. OA raids three times a week, and if FR is one of their primary raid targets, given the competitive nature of the Eles, and the number of guilds involved in those gods, they may waste a good raid on a lesser mob. <br /><br />So really in the grand scheme of things, it wasnt a big deal. But i mean really the position is indefensible, how can you say wasting a mob for lower guilds is ok because you were testing yourself? Go kill Tunat or MM if you are looking for a challenge, the lower guilds need those mobs.
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
